.TH LIBDAQ_ALERT_CPP 3 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-bigredbox 2.0.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
libdaq_alert_cpp, mu2e::daq::AlertSender \- C++ library for sending Big Red Box alerts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <daq_alert.hpp>
.PP
.B namespace mu2e { namespace daq {
.PP
.B class AlertError : public std::runtime_error { ... };
.PP
.B class AlertSender {
.B public:
.BI "    explicit AlertSender(std::string " broadcast_ip " = \(dq255.255.255.255\(dq,"
.BI "                         uint16_t " port " = 37020);"
.BI "    void send(const std::string &" system_id ,
.BI "              const std::string &" message ") const;"
.BI "    static void send_once(const std::string &" system_id ,
.BI "                          const std::string &" message ,
.BI "                          const std::string &" broadcast_ip " = \(dq255.255.255.255\(dq,"
.BI "                          uint16_t " port " = 37020);"
.B "    const std::string &broadcast_ip() const;"
.B "    uint16_t           port() const;"
.B };
.PP
.B }}
.fi
.PP
Link with
.B \-ldaq_alert_cpp \-ldaq_alert
(CMake target
.BR daq_alert_cpp ,
which links
.B daq_alert_c
publicly).
C++17.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B AlertSender
stores a destination address and port.
.B send()
calls
.BR daq_alert_send (3)
with them and throws
.B AlertError
carrying
.BR daq_alert_strerror (3)
text on any non\-zero result.
.B send_once()
constructs a temporary sender and sends one alert.
.PP
Every call goes through the C library, so the datagram bytes, the
timestamp format, the field size limit and the address handling are exactly
those of
.BR libdaq_alert (3).
Strings containing an embedded NUL are truncated at the NUL by
.BR c_str() .
.PP
The object has no mutable state after construction; a const instance may be
shared between threads.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B mu2e::daq::AlertError
Socket creation or
.BR sendto (2)
failed, or a field was too long
.RB ( DAQ_ALERT_ERR_FORMAT ).
.PP
An address that is not a dotted quad does
.B not
throw: it is sent as a limited broadcast (see
.BR libdaq_alert (3),
.BR NOTES ).
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS 4
.nf
#include <daq_alert.hpp>
#include <iostream>

void on_fatal(const std::string &what)
{
    static const mu2e::daq::AlertSender sender;   // 255.255.255.255:37020
    try {
        sender.send("DAQ\-NODE\-01", what);
    } catch (const mu2e::daq::AlertError &e) {
        std::cerr << "alert failed: " << e.what() << '\en';
    }
}
.fi
.RE
